{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>As Aaron your brother was gathered.</b> From here that Moses craved the death of Aaron (there). Another interpretation: you are no better than he — ״because you did not sanctify Me״ (Deuteronomy 32:51); but if you had sanctified Me, your time to depart had still not arrived (there). Everywhere Scripture writes their death, it writes their sin, because a decree was decreed upon the wilderness generation to die in the wilderness for the sin that they did not believe; therefore Moses asked that Scripture write his sin, so they would not say: he too was among the rebels. A parable: two women being flogged in court — one sinned, and one ate unripe produce of the seventh year, etc. So too here, everywhere He mentioned their death, He mentioned their sin, to make known that there was nothing in them but this alone (Yoma ch. 6)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:01.800595537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}